    "scenesThatPass": [
      "DAISY: I'm gone to the market, Idella.\nIDELLA: Mmmrnmm. Daisy heads out the door.",
      "FLORINE: Hey, Mother Werthan! It's just us! ON DAISY, appearing at the landing, a book in her hand.\nDAISY: Why didn't you call?\nFLORINE: We can't stay.\nDAISY: So I gather.",
      "FLORINE: I had these made. Doesn't your baby look cute?\nDAISY: That's not exactly the word I'd pick.",
      "LIBRARIAN: I've got that Revolutionary War book you were asking about, Miz Werthan. I put it aside for you.\nDAISY: You're a sweet thing, Miss Jensen.\nLIBRARIAN: Everybody's just crazy about it!\nDAISY: Well, thank you very much.",
      "IDELLA: I'm gone, Miz Daisy.\nDAISY: All right, Idella. See you tomorrow."
    ]
